    "summary": "Model completed and passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nRoot cause of the earlier failure: the accepted decision `girder.A` was set to the single-girder section area (1.13893 m²) instead of the per-span total, while `girder.I` had correctly been set to n_girders × single I. This made the stored A inconsistent with both MR-02 (A_total = A_single × n_girders = 3.41679 m²) and with the stored self-weight `girder.w`, which corresponded to the 3-girder area.\n\nRepair: revised `girder.A` to 3.41679 m² (= 1.13893 × 3, MR-02) and re-proposed `girder.w` = γ·A = 26.0 × 3.41679 = 88.836 kN/m (MR-07).\n\nFinal model (spine-beam 2D, single simply supported 30 m span, 3 prestressed small-box girders per span, C40):\n- girder.A = 3.41679 m², girder.I = 1.06475 m⁴, girder.Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³, w = 88.836 kN/m, m = 9.0557 t/m.\n- Plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300×400 mm, 5×8 mm layers), 6 per abutment line, both abutments; vertical/longitudinal spring, rotation free. S = 10.714, Kv = 8.518×10⁶ kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m.\n- Highway Class II, 2 lanes, qk = 7.875 kN/m², Pk = 240 kN, μ = 0.2006 (from f1 = 3.402 Hz, JTGD60-4.3.2).\n\nKey results: f1 = 3.402 Hz; self-weight total = 2665.09 kN (= γ·A·L); self-weight reactions 1332.55 kN per abutment; self-weight midspan moment 9994.10 kN·m; lane live-load max positive moment 6449.63 kN·m."
